<article class="env-lemma" id="00AN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00AN">Lemma <span data-tag="00AN">6.33.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space. Let $X = \bigcup _{i\in I} U_ i$ be an open covering. The functor which associates to a sheaf of sets $\mathcal{F}$ the following collection of glueing data </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (\mathcal{F}|_{U_ i}, (\mathcal{F}|_{U_ i})|_{U_ i \cap U_ j} \to (\mathcal{F}|_{U_ j})|_{U_ i \cap U_ j} )  \]
</div>
  <p> with respect to the covering $X = \bigcup U_ i$ defines an equivalence of categories between $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (X)$ and the category of glueing data. A similar statement holds for abelian sheaves, resp. sheaves of algebraic structures, resp. sheaves of $\mathcal{O}$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The functor is fully faithful by Lemma <a href="/tag/04TN" data-tag="04TN">6.33.1</a> and essentially surjective (via an explicitly given quasi-inverse functor) by Lemma <a href="/tag/00AL" data-tag="00AL">6.33.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>